    "updated_at": "2025-06-10T00:46:36Z",
    "body": "> 1. The value expected by the reporting API is not an URL string, but rather an endpoint as defined (and sent separately) in https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/HTTP/Reference/Headers/Reporting-Endpoints\n\nThanks for catching this! A PR is welcome to fix it.\n\n> 2\\. The reporting API defines specific objects for the report body - such as [CSPViolationReportBody](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/API/CSPViolationReportBody). Would it be possible for the HTML spec to similarly define an object name.\n\nThis is not possible. The use of IDL for other reporting API endpoints is a mistake, as those are not constructors we want to expose to JavaScript. They should not really have names at all.\n\nhttps://github.com/w3c/reporting/pull/258 is working on removing all the existing classes.",
