    "body": "Thank you\n\n> Thanks for catching this! A PR is welcome to fix it.\n\nAttempted in #11366\n\n> This is not possible. The use of IDL for other reporting API endpoints is a mistake, as those are not constructors we want to expose to JavaScript. They should not really have names at all.\n\n@domenic So the https://github.com/w3c/reporting/pull/258 says \n\n>   A <dfn id=dom-report dictionary>Report</dfn> is the application-exposed representation of a <a>report</a>.\n> <dfn id=\"reportbody\" dictionary>ReportBody</dfn> is an abstract dictionary  type from which specific report types should inherit.\n\nDoesn't that mean that new report dictionaries are _expected_ to be created?\nSo instead of `CSPViolationReportBody` I'd expect the spec to define `CSPViolationReport` (or similar)? That doesn't appear to be part of the change here, so perhaps it is incomplete?\n\nBut anyway, to me the name is what is important as this allows us to clearly change-control the object in browser compatibility data and MDN doc  Or to put it another way \"can we have `COEPViolationReport` dictionary defined\" or whatever this new object will be for a report?\n\n",
    "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
