    "created_at": "2026-09-14T13:54:27Z",
    "updated_at": "2026-09-14T13:54:27Z",
    "body": "In addition to correcting the prose regarding \"valid URL string\", there is also a Structured Fields type discrepancy (`token` vs. `string`) to consider.\n\nReporting endpoints configured via `Reporting-Endpoints` are named by dictionary keys (`sf-key`), which are a subset of `sf-token`. Other specifications referencing reporting endpoints (such as `Permissions-Policy` and `Document-Policy`, see [WICG/document-policy#47](https://github.com/WICG/document-policy/issues/47)) specify and parse `report-to` as a `token` (e.g., `report-to=endpoint`).\n\nHowever, the COOP parsing algorithm currently requires a `string`, while COEP has no type check:\n* Neither [WebKit](https://github.com/WebKit/WebKit/blob/main/Source/WebCore/Modules/reporting/ReportingScope.cpp#L156-L159) nor [Chromium](https://source.chromium.org/chromium/chromium/src/+/main:content/browser/security/coop/cross_origin_opener_policy_reporter.cc;l=281) uses the parsed value as a URI; both use it strictly as an endpoint name to look up the destination URL from `Reporting-Endpoints`.\n* But because the spec and WPTs used strings, both [WebKit](https://github.com/WebKit/WebKit/blob/main/Source/WebCore/loader/CrossOriginOpenerPolicy.cpp#L240) ([COEP](https://github.com/WebKit/WebKit/blob/main/Source/WebCore/loader/CrossOriginEmbedderPolicy.cpp#L61)) and [Chromium](https://source.chromium.org/chromium/chromium/src/+/main:services/network/public/cpp/cross_origin_opener_policy_parser.cc;l=82) ([COEP](https://source.chromium.org/chromium/chromium/src/+/main:services/network/public/cpp/cross_origin_embedder_policy_parser.cc;l=37)) currently parse `report-to` exclusively as a string (`.getIf<String>()` / `.GetIfString()`), rejecting unquoted tokens.\n\nWe should update the spec prose to specify `report-to` as a `token` to align with the rest of the platform, but update the parsing algorithms to accept either a `token` or a `string` (`and it is a token or a string`) for backwards-compatibility with deployed headers and existing implementations.",
    "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
